Third-party data:

The per-language comment and string syntax declarations in spells/comments.go
adopt the schema of, and seed their values from, languages.json in scc
(github.com/boyter/scc), copyright Ben Boyter, licensed under the MIT License.
Only the entries for languages magus ships spells for are included.

The embedding table libs/embed pins in gen/table.digest is converted from
potion-code-16M-v2 (huggingface.co/minishlab/potion-code-16M-v2, revision
e9d2a44ca6a05ac6685f3b23709ea57eb7352d5b), copyright MinishLab (Stephan Tulkens
and Thomas van Dongen), licensed under the MIT License, and built with model2vec
(github.com/MinishLab/model2vec), also MIT. MinishLab distilled potion from
nomic-ai/CodeRankEmbed, itself MIT-licensed, and trained it on the CornStack
code corpus. The table is redistributed through an OCI artifact, not in the
magus binary.

